# Mini-app version + release notes

Whenever you ship **user-facing** changes in `shiori.cloud` (UI, features, fixes users will notice), before commit/push:

1. **Bump** `package.json` `version` (semver: patch for fixes/small UI, minor for features).
2. **Add** a matching entry at the top of `src/data/releaseNotes.ts` with the same `version`, optional `title`, and Persian `items`.
3. Do **not** skip this for “just a small fix” if it affects the mini-app experience.
4. Pure docs/chore/CI-only changes: no bump needed.

## Writing notes (user-facing)

- Keep **at most ~3** short bullets; benefit language, not engineering detail.
- Bad: «رفع فلیکر پوستر هنگام جابه‌جایی روزها»
- Good: «برنامهٔ پخش روان‌تر شد»
- Set `showDialog: true` **only** when the update is worth interrupting the user (usually minor/major or a clearly noticeable feature).
- Day-to-day patches: omit `showDialog` (silent bump; still listed in Profile → «چی جدید شده؟»).
- During heavy beta, set `VITE_SHOW_RELEASE_NOTES=false` so the popup stays off; archive still works.

```ts
// src/data/releaseNotes.ts — newest first
{
  version: '0.2.8', // must match package.json
  title: '…',
  // showDialog: true, // only for important updates
  items: ['…', '…'],
}
```

The post-splash dialog shows at most the newest unseen note with `showDialog: true` when `VITE_APP_VERSION` > last acknowledged version in `localStorage` and `VITE_SHOW_RELEASE_NOTES` is not false.
